Native libraries vendored by psycopg[binary]
--------------------------------------------

durable-llm depends on `psycopg[binary]`, which installs the psycopg-binary wheel. That wheel
does not link against a system libpq -- it ships its own copy of libpq together with the
transitive native stack libpq needs:

  libpq          (PostgreSQL client library)  PostgreSQL Licence
  OpenSSL 3      (libssl, libcrypto)          Apache-2.0
  MIT Kerberos 5 (libgssapi_krb5, libkrb5,    MIT-style (MIT Kerberos licence)
                  libk5crypto, libcom_err)
  OpenLDAP       (libldap, liblber)           OpenLDAP Public License

These are compiled shared objects inside the Python package. Python-level vulnerability
scanners -- pip-audit, `uv pip audit`, Dependabot on requirements/lock files, and anything
else that works from PyPI package names and versions -- resolve `psycopg-binary==3.3.4`
and stop there. They do not enumerate the vendored libraries and therefore report no
findings for an OpenSSL or Kerberos CVE that is present in the wheel. A quiet report from
those tools is not evidence that the native stack is patched.

Operators who need native-library CVE tracking should install plain `psycopg` (without the
`binary` extra) built against a system libpq, so that OpenSSL, Kerberos, and OpenLDAP come
from the OS package manager and are covered by the OS vulnerability feed and its updates.
That path requires libpq and a build toolchain to be present; the binary wheel exists to
avoid exactly that, which is why it is the default here and why this trade-off is written
down rather than assumed.


Optional `anthropic` extra
--------------------------

`pip install durable-llm[anthropic]` pulls in the Anthropic SDK and its transitive closure. All
of it is permissive, but the spread is wider than MIT alone -- notably certifi, which is
weak-copyleft:

  certifi              MPL-2.0                 (also bundles the Mozilla CA root store)
  anthropic            MIT
  anyio                MIT
  docstring-parser     MIT
  jiter                MIT
  pydantic             MIT
  pydantic-core        MIT
  annotated-types      MIT
  typing-inspection    MIT
  h11                  MIT
  httpx                BSD-3-Clause
  httpcore             BSD-3-Clause
  idna                 BSD-3-Clause
  distro               Apache-2.0
  sniffio              MIT OR Apache-2.0
  typing-extensions    PSF-2.0

MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft: it constrains modifications to certifi's own files, not
code that merely imports it. The core of durable-llm does not install any of these -- the
provider adapters are optional on purpose, so a deployment that only uses the `echo`
provider carries the psycopg licences and nothing else.


Development-only dependencies
-----------------------------

pytest, ruff, and their transitive dependencies are in the `dev` dependency group, not in
any published extra. They are not installed by `pip install durable-llm` and are not part of
durable-llm's distributable surface, so they are not enumerated here.
